  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Equalities FCDO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FCDO has commissioned Plan International UK, working with Consortium partners Sightsavers and Social Development Direct (SDDirect) to design and lead the implementation of a four-year Gender and Equalities (G&amp;E) Capability Development Programme, running from 2023&#x2013;27, with the possibility of extension. This will be managed by the Gender and Equalities team at FCDO but will seek to engage broadly both internally within FCDO (both in the UK and globally) and externally with key stakeholders, to strengthen capabilities across Gender and Equalities thematics._x000d_
In summary, the programme aims to develop a more coherent approach to gender and equalities across the FCDO, bringing together the best of diplomacy and development, and building more consistent capacity through access to support and resources across all gender and equality thematics and across all FCDO regions (Latin America, Africa, MENA, and Asia). In addition, the programme will enable FCDO to showcase and disseminate its resources and tools to external audiences._x000d_
This approach responds to critical areas including growing inequalities and the rollback in the rights of women and marginalised groups, opportunities and increased demand created through the FCDO merger, and ensuring best value for money through ODA investments. The intended impact is to contribute towards building a safer, more equitable and prosperous world, where everyone can fulfil their potential, realise their rights and be free from discrimination. _x000d_
The indicative high-level outcomes shown in the theory of change (ToC) diagram below are designed to enable the FCDO to maintain and further strengthen their ability to progress gender and equalities influence and programming:_x000d_
&#x2022;	Strong regional networks and partnerships to work effectively to challenge and change policy and practice to increase equalities._x000d_
&#x2022;	FCDO at posts and external partners at national levels, use their positions of power and influence, policy tools and ODA programming (where appropriate) to create environments that support women and girls, and marginalised groups including LGBTQI+ and persons with disabilities to thrive, and support reversal of rollback of these groups rights. _x000d_
&#x2022;	Broader discourse in regions is further shifted towards gender and equalities issues including through empowering civil society organisations and networks.</narrative>
  </description>
